<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsewang Rabtan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1643–1727</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsewang Rabtan was ruler of the Dzungar Khanate from 1697 until his death in 1727. A nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galdan-boshugtu-khan">Galdan Boshugtu Khan</a>, he restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> power after Galdan's defeat by the Qing, fought the Qing and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, and in 1717 sent an army that took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a>. His invasion of the Kazakh Khanate in 1723 is remembered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a> as the Great Disaster.</p></div>
